# sudoers rule for the server-manager service user (svmgr).
#
# Allows svmgr to invoke ONLY the game-unitctl wrapper (start/stop), with no
# password. Status checks (`systemctl is-active`) need no privileges and are
# NOT listed here on purpose.
#
# Why this goes through a wrapper instead of a `systemctl start/stop <unit>`
# rule directly: sudo-rs (Ubuntu's default sudo since 26.04) rejects
# wildcards anywhere in a command's ARGUMENTS — the previous rule, which
# matched the unit-name argument with a trailing wildcard (`game-` prefix,
# `.service` suffix, `*` in between), is a syntax error under sudo-rs
# (`wildcards are not allowed in command arguments`), even though classic
# sudo accepted it as a glob. The only wildcard sudo-rs supports in
# arguments is a bare `*` as the FINAL argument, meaning "zero or more
# subsequent arguments" (matches the header comment in deploy/game-unitctl).
# So instead of matching the unit name in sudoers, the app now invokes a
# fixed, validated wrapper (deploy/game-unitctl) that does that same
# unit-name check itself. sudoers itself does not bound the argument list at
# all here — it is the WRAPPER that only ever forwards its own $1 (verb) and
# $2 (unit) to systemctl, ignoring anything beyond that. This form is also
# accepted by classic sudo, so one file covers both.
#
# APPLY BOTH the wrapper (deploy/game-unitctl, installed to
# /usr/local/sbin/game-unitctl) AND this file BEFORE deploying the app build
# that invokes the wrapper: deploying the app first (with the wrapper or this
# rule missing) makes every start/stop fail immediately, since sudo would
# reject or fail to find the command.
#
# There are no bare/rollback-compatibility lines here for an older app build
# that still calls `systemctl` directly: under sudo-rs, a single invalid line
# (e.g. the old trailing-wildcard rule described above) makes the ENTIRE
# sudoers file invalid, so the old wildcard rule cannot be kept alongside
# this one. Rolling back the app to a pre-wrapper build requires reverting
# this file too.
#
# Install:
#   1. Install the wrapper FIRST: sudo cp game-unitctl /usr/local/sbin/game-unitctl
#                                  sudo chown root:root /usr/local/sbin/game-unitctl
#                                  sudo chmod 0755 /usr/local/sbin/game-unitctl
#   2. Copy this file:            sudo cp sudoers.d-example /etc/sudoers.d/server-manager
#   3. Fix permissions:           sudo chmod 0440 /etc/sudoers.d/server-manager
#   4. ALWAYS validate:           sudo visudo -c
#      (a broken file in /etc/sudoers.d can lock you out of sudo entirely)

svmgr ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/game-unitctl start *, /usr/local/sbin/game-unitctl stop *
